4381.stem:
On another planet, a ball is launched vertically into the air from the ground.

The height above the ground, $h$ metres, can be modelled using the function $h = -6t^2 + 24t$, where $t$ is measured in seconds. The graph of the function is shown.

\exfigure{300_q20_1}

parts.latex:
An object is projected vertically into the air. Its height, $h$ metres, above the ground after $t$ seconds is given by $h = -5t^2 + 80t$.

\exfigure{271_q9_1}

For how long is the object at a height of 300 metres or more above the ground?

4497.stem:
A fence is to be built around the outside of a rectangular paddock. An internal fence is also to be built.

The side lengths of the paddock are $x$ metres and $y$ metres, as shown in the diagram.

\exfigure{36_q19_1}

A total of 900 metres of fencing is to be used. Therefore $3x + 2y = 900$.

The area, $A$, in square metres, of the rectangular paddock is given by $A = 450x - 1.5x^2$. The graph of this equation is shown.

\exfigure{36_q19_2}

5972.stem:
A rectangle has width $w$ centimetres. The area of the rectangle, $A$, in square centimetres, is $A = 2w^2 + 5w$.

The graph of $A = 2w^2 + 5w$ is shown.

\exfigure{5832_q31_1}
